cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MetaFOCUS in academic work, please cite the MetaFOCUS paper:
  Verhoeven, G. J., Ressl, C., and Wieser, M. (2026). MetaFOCUS: a Python
  Toolbox for Optimising, Characterising, and Understanding
  Structure-from-Motion Pipelines in Agisoft Metashape Professional. 9th
  ISPRS Low-Cost 3D Workshop, Braunschweig, Germany, 18–20 November 2026.
type: software
title: "MetaFOCUS: Metashape Functions for Optimising, Characterising, and Understanding Structure from Motion"
abstract: >-
  A toolbox of Python scripts for Agisoft Metashape Professional. It provides
  control-measurement diagnostics, structure-from-motion (SfM) process
  analysis, filtering and project management, and surface-derived outputs,
  such as image footprints and the ground sampling distance (GSD).
